 This matrix is not invertible if and only if its determinant is 0:
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{vmatrix}

&= \begin{vmatrix} c & a \\ a & b \end{vmatrix} - \begin{vmatrix} b & a \\ c & b \end{vmatrix} + \begin{vmatrix} b & c \\ c & a \end{vmatrix} \\
&= (cb - a^2) - (b^2 - ac) + (ab - c^2) \\ &= 0.
\end{align*}Then
\[-a^2 - b^2 - c^2 + ab + ac + bc = 0.\]Multiplying everything by 2, we get
\[2ab + 2ac + 2bc - 2a^2 - 2b^2 - 2c^2 = 0.\]Then
\[a^2 - 2ab + b^2 + b^2 - 2ac + c^2 + c^2 - 2bc + a^2 = 0.\]In other words,
\begin{align*}
(a - b)^2 + (b - c)^2 + (c - a)^2 &= 0.
\end{align*}Since each of these squares is nonnegative, they must all be 0, so $a = b = c.$

Hence,
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b} = \frac{a}{2a} + \frac{a}{2a} + \frac{a}{2a} ... = \frac{3}{2}.\]Therefore, the $\boxed{ \EE }$ only value of the expression is $\frac{3}{2}.$
Note: This is because the matrix in the problem is symmetric with respect to the three variables.  Similar matrices are orthogonal, so the matrix is similar to a matrix of the form
\[\begin{pmatrix} d & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & d & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & d \end{pmatrix},\]which is not invertible.  Hence, any matrix
\[\begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{pmatrix}\] -=- is invertible if and only if $a + b + c = 0.$

